==Evolution==
Evolves into '''True Killer Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Radical Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
This is a <u>joke character</u>. He has the exact same stats as [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], but an insanely high cost (tied with [[Killer Tank Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Tank Cat]], [[Killer Gross Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Gross Cat]], and [[Killer Cowbird Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Cowbird Cat]] for the highest in the game), which makes it, by far, the least cost-efficient cat you could ever use in a stage. Due to this, he is only good for [[User Rank]], [[Cat Combo]]s and grinding [[Meow Medals]].

Using him with [[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss]] and [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]] will activate one of the best Research Combos in the game: [[Bad Guys (Combo)|Bad Guys]]. This Combo decreases recharge times by 79f (2.63 seconds); it works very well with units such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]. Killer Cat's other Combo is [[Black & White (Combo)|Black & White]], which is a Worker Cat Max Up (Sm) Combo that requires only him and the [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Basic Cat]]. This combo also has a synergy with [[Rich and Poor (Combo)|Rich & Poor]], and is very useful in timed stages. This is especially helpful for the [[Ranking Dojo]].

For obvious reasons, it is not recommended to use the [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]] with him in your lineup, as all he does is drain money.

Otherwise, you can use Killer Cat for User Rank, as his upgrade costs aren't very high for a Rare unit.

==='''True Form'''===
After a very long time, Killer Cat's True Form gives this unit proper stats, making him a solid option for tanking [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] and [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies. His recharge speed isn't the best, and his price is still quite high for a meatshield, but he is effective at what he can do for his price (especially compared to before). He has decent DPS for a meatshield, but due to his 3 knockbacks, this isn't the ideal use for him. Instead, he serves as a counter against [[Pterowl Hazuku]], as it's a Floating/Behemoth enemy with the ability to create [[Surge Attack|Surges]]. Additionally, Radical Cat does decently well against [[Ensanglion the Calamity]], as it can survive a hit at just Lv.38. The [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]] ability is alright, but it's more of a bonus than a selling point of the unit. Tragically, due to how Hazuku and other Floating enemies are usually mixed in with other traits, Radical Cat may not be as useful as he seems, though he can still be a serviceable meatshield against his targeted traits.

Additionally, his recharge speed can be greatly helped by the Bad Guys Cat Combo, substantially increasing the rate at which you can send him out and making stalling Behemoth and Floating enemies much easier.

Combo-wise, Radical Cat gains a new combo with [[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Hevijak]] and [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]] for a defense up medium. This can be very useful for black/floating centered behemoth levels, and if Bad Guys is acquired, specialized meatshields such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen]], [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong]], and even Radical and Gas Mask themselves gain a great defense boost along with much faster recharging, allowing for much better stalling  against their targeted traits.

